e only when no other eligible choice supplies a useful comparator. For an incomplete-only answer, choose leads whose reported date, seats, fees or program show a useful next-check contrast; these remain leads, never complete itineraries. Preserve unknown price scope, traveler support and separate-ticket protection. The writer sees only the selected source facts, so retain material comparison evidence. The exact_details index supplies source-bound journey_components, per-journey separate-booking waits, factored award-itinerary connections, and component original-currency quotes in major units. Use these exact references to distinguish within-award layovers from separate-ticket connection waits; they have different risk meanings. Compare reported fee and cash amounts using the display value and currency, never mental division of raw minor units. A quote with unknown price_scope is neither per traveler nor a party total, even if returned traveler evidence is known. Unknown wait_minutes is not zero. Keep a comparator when its exact buffer, schedule, cabin or quote changes the decision; no fixed count applies.\nWrite for the traveler. Call the supplied material search results, not a packet or an internal validation workflow.",
